"""Deli Counter 0.248.0 (the factory's roadmap 281): an office building's open floor is an office.

`floor` is a shop-floor word, so the office preset's 816 m2 `floor_1` -- office's and office_stepped's open storey over
the bullpen -- was furnished by the shop floor's recipe, and cold run 9369's frame showed litter bins standing mid-floor
among cartons. `level_design.is_office_floor` reads it on the card shop's terms: a building whose id says `office`, a
room the word table would make a shop floor by `floor` alone; `_room_kind` asks it after the video store's rule.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has
been worked out: `level_design.py` (anchored hunks); office's and office_stepped's specs, refurnished, carried whole;
the new `test_office_floor_kind.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a proven clone
(`patches/dc_office_floor/gen_dc_office_floor.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a second run
refused (`patches/dc_office_floor/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_office_floor.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
